       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to **7,650 mg/day**. That is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of 2,550 mg/day (the FDA-labeled maximum for immediate-release). A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day total.\n- **2,550 mg total per day**, divided differently, such as 1,275 mg twice daily.\n- A lower dose, since many patients start at 500 mg once or twice daily and titrate up.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 2550 mg three times daily as written, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest adding a note with the rationale."
