       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 7,650 mg/day is three times the maximum daily dose, and I can't identify a therapeutic reason for it. Metformin doses above 2,550 mg/day add no glycemic benefit, and they greatly raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function. Entering it could directly harm the patient.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum).\n- A lower or titrated regimen, such as 500 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n\nIf there's a specific clinical reason for the higher dose, I'd recommend discussing it with pharmacy. They can review it and enter it through their own verification process.\n\nWhich of the options above would you like me to enter?"
